{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Who has wrought and made.</b> Like the usage of תקון, as in וימהר לעשות אותו (Genesis 18:7). The meaning: Who has wrought this — HaShem made it, that is, He calls the generations from the outset before they come to be. The meaning is that He knows all the generations that will arrive, and He calls each generation to stand in its time:" "<b>I am YHWH.</b> The first to all the generations that have passed, and with the last ones I am He:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {0 "Resolved the unpointed יי in the lemma as YHWH, rendered per voice rules."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:20.789124700Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}